  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q22-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "22",
    "prompt": "Before church, every parishioner shakes hands with every other parishioner. The priest arrives late and only shakes hands with some of the parishioners. In total, there are 1400 handshakes. How many hands does the priest shake?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "22 hands.\n\nThere are 53 parishioners; subtract their 1378 handshakes from 1400.",
      "worked": "Let $n$ be the number of parishioners and $h$ the number of hands the priest shakes. Counting each pair once, the parishioners contribute\n$$\\begin{align*}H&=1+2+\\cdots+(n-1)\\\\H&=\\frac{n(n-1)}{2}.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $0\\le h\\le n$,\n$$\\begin{align*}h&=1400-\\frac{n(n-1)}{2},\\\\0&\\le1400-\\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\le n.\\end{align*}$$\nHence $n(n-1)\\le2800$ and $n(n+1)\\ge2800$. If $n\\le52$, then $n(n+1)\\le52\\times53=2756$. If $n\\ge54$, then $n(n-1)\\ge54\\times53=2862$. Therefore $n=53$.\n$$\\begin{align*}h&=1400-\\frac{53\\times52}{2}\\\\h&=1400-1378\\\\h&=22.\\end{align*}$$\nThe priest shakes 22 hands.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 85
  },
